Hello!

How would you say 'solve et coagula' in lojban? It is a Latin alchemical 
motto, obviously meaning 'solve and coagulate' or 'divide and join' -- 1st 
person imperative. I've found 'fendi' and 'jorne' but don't know how to put 
them in a phrase. I don't speak any lojban.

It's for the name of a boat. A packraft, to be precise. I do like the Latin 
phrase, but when push comes to shove I'd prefer a still more universal and 
less imperialist language.

Thank you in advance!

